# Week 10: GeoPandas exploration, join and maps

## Overview
In this week, I used GeoPandas to load, inspect, spatially join, and map my custom Patani project data.

## Scripts Created
* `my_explore.py`: Loaded `Patani ward.gpkg` and printed layer geometry, shape, bounds, and CRS.
* `my_points.py`: Loaded the settlement GeoPackage and verified point alignment with wards.
* `my_join.py`: Performed spatial join between settlements and wards.
* `my_make_map.py`: Generated and saved `patani_settlement_map.png`.
* `my_save_output.py`: Exported layers to `week10_outputs.gpkg` and tables to CSV.

## Reflection
Working with GeoPandas made it straightforward to inspect spatial properties and generate maps directly from Python scripts.